listenT -- the listener with no onNotify (Tony, 2026-11-05, R1, R2 and the fixture ruling). A field that names
listenTo:=x gets x's VALUE on every write to x, and nothing else of x's.

Row by row, in pop.sh:
  LN-1 three writes reach the listener; the opening 1 is its own value at define (a dead listener reads 1 1 1 1).
  LN-2 the listener's own attribute survives a notify, and none of the notifier's arrives, with the value moved beside them.
  LN-3 one write to lnA reaches lnC through lnB.
  LN-4 the copy never reports "set group to itself".

